  "body": "## Gap\n\nA closed LWPOLYLINE with two distinct vertices and two straight segments traces the same span twice. Adjacent LINE and ARC entities can use that span to form a valid perimeter. The ordinary chain graph counts both edges and can report a junction. Its refusal is correct for the original graph.\n\n## Requested behavior\n\nLet the operator select a single traversal of that exact source span for a profile. Keep the original drawing and both occurrences. Identify the selected source or chain across save and reopen. Never combine unrelated coincident entities or select a path at a remaining fork.\n\nUse a synthetic drawing with a retraced straight span and an adjacent mixed line and arc path. Check the derived closed loop and its direction. Refuse a zero-length edge, competing branches, a changed source, a nonzero polyline bulge and a self-intersecting result. Keep normal import and its diagnostics available.\n\n#1861 covers normal chaining and branch refusal. #2022 covers selecting wire chains. This issue covers an explicit choice when repeated geometry prevents that chain from forming. #3176 covers the import of drawing metadata.\n\nSuggested labels: enhancement, P6, effort:max, area:2d, source:agent.\n",
